You are reviewing two first-run pages, X and Y, for a GNU/Linux USB stick handed to newcomers in a volunteer organizing group. The page is the first thing a newcomer sees: one window, plain choices, usable with a mouse alone.
Score each page 1 to 5 on: (a) plain language a newcomer understands; (b) usable with a mouse alone and with a keyboard alone; (c) accessibility: follows the system light/dark setting, readable contrast, semantic HTML, labels; (d) honesty: it does not promise things it cannot do; (e) simplicity: no heavy framework, small.
Then say which page you would hand a newcomer, and the single most important fix for each.
Answer in JSON only: {"X":{"a":n,"b":n,"c":n,"d":n,"e":n,"fix":"..."},"Y":{...},"prefer":"X or Y","why":"one sentence"}

=== X ===
<!doctype html>
<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'">
<title>Welcome</title>
<style>
/* Light is the complete default. Dark follows the computer unless the person chose light;
   a person who chose dark gets it either way. The two dark sets must stay identical (lr1ck checks).
   Each colour names the Modus theme value it copies (lr1ck reads Emacs' own copy and compares). */
:root{
  --bg:#ffffff;     /* modus:bg-main */
  --card:#f0f0f0;   /* modus:bg-alt */
  --fg:#000000;     /* modus:fg-main */
  --muted:#505050;  /* modus:fg-alt */
  --accent:#0031a9; /* modus:blue */
  --line:#56576d;   /* modus:fg-unfocused */
  --focus:#0031a9;  /* modus:blue */
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --bg:#000000;     /* modus:bg-main */
    --card:#191a1b;   /* modus:bg-alt */
    --fg:#ffffff;     /* modus:fg-main */
    --muted:#a8a8a8;  /* modus:fg-alt */
    --accent:#2fafff; /* modus:blue */
    --line:#93959b;   /* modus:fg-unfocused */
    --focus:#2fafff;  /* modus:blue */
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#000000;     /* modus:bg-main */
  --card:#191a1b;   /* modus:bg-alt */
  --fg:#ffffff;     /* modus:fg-main */
  --muted:#a8a8a8;  /* modus:fg-alt */
  --accent:#2fafff; /* modus:blue */
  --line:#93959b;   /* modus:fg-unfocused */
  --focus:#2fafff;  /* modus:blue */
}
html{color-scheme:light dark}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:1.125rem/1.5 system-ui,"Segoe UI","DejaVu Sans",sans-serif}
main{max-width:44rem;margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem}
h1{font-size:2rem;margin:.5rem 0}
h2{font-size:1.4rem;margin:1.5rem 0 .5rem}
ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.75rem}
[hidden]{display:none!important}
body:not([data-edition="author"]) .author-only{display:none}
.choice{display:block;min-height:4.5rem;padding:1rem 1.25rem;border:2px solid var(--line);border-radius:.75rem;background:var(--card);color:var(--fg);text-decoration:none}
.choice:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}
.choice:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:4px solid var(--focus);outline-offset:3px}
.label{display:block;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent)}
.plain{display:block}
.theme{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin:1.5rem 0 0}
button{min-height:3rem;padding:.5rem 1rem;border:2px solid var(--line);border-radius:.5rem;background:var(--card);color:var(--fg);font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
button[aria-pressed="true"]{border-color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
footer{margin-top:1.5rem;color:var(--muted)}
</style>
</head>
<body data-profile="desktop" data-edition="base">
<main>
<h1>Welcome</h1>
<p>Pick one. You can come back to this page whenever you like.</p>
<ul id="choices">
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="*"><a class="choice" href="larder:try" data-choice="try"><span class="label">Look around first</span><span class="plain">Nothing you do here is kept when you turn the computer off.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="*"><a class="choice" href="larder:private" data-choice="private"><span class="label">Make my private space</span><span class="plain">You choose a PIN. Your files stay on this stick, locked.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="*"><a class="choice" href="larder:chapter" data-choice="chapter"><span class="label">Join my group</span><span class="plain">Connect to your group's server, using the file a facilitator gave you.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="desktop hardened fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:library" data-choice="library"><span class="label">Open the library</span><span class="plain">Read books and guides without the internet.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="desktop hardened fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:write" data-choice="write"><span class="label">Write a document</span><span class="plain">Open a word processor.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="base" data-profiles="*"><a class="choice" href="larder:help" data-choice="help"><span class="label">Ask for help</span><span class="plain">Someone you trust can see your screen, only while you allow it. You can stop at any time.</span></a></li>
</ul>
<section class="author-only">
<h2>Books and stories</h2>
<ul id="author-choices">
<li data-edition-only="author" data-profiles="desktop fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:read" data-choice="read"><span class="label">Read a book</span><span class="plain">Open the book reader.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="author" data-profiles="desktop fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:listen" data-choice="listen"><span class="label">Listen to a book</span><span class="plain">Play an audiobook from this stick.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="author" data-profiles="desktop fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:fanwork" data-choice="fanwork"><span class="label">Write a fan work</span><span class="plain">Start a new story in this world.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="author" data-profiles="desktop fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:stamp" data-choice="stamp"><span class="label">Mark my story by permission</span><span class="plain">Adds the notice's mark to a finished story. It refuses until the author has signed the notice.</span></a></li>
<li data-edition-only="author" data-profiles="desktop fullsink"><a class="choice" href="larder:notice" data-choice="notice"><span class="label">Read the permission notice</span><span class="plain">What you may and may not do with these stories.</span></a></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="theme" role="group" aria-label="Colours">
<button type="button" data-theme-choice="system">Follow my computer</button>
<button type="button" data-theme-choice="light">Light</button>
<button type="button" data-theme-choice="dark">Dark</button>
</div>
<footer><p>Edition: <span id="edition-name">desktop</span>. This page does not contact the internet.</p></footer>
</main>
<script>
(function () {
  var b = document.body, p = b.dataset.profile, e = b.dataset.edition, r = document.documentElement;
  var each = function (list, f) { Array.prototype.forEach.call(list, f); };
  document.getElementById("edition-name").textContent = p + (e === "author" ? " (author edition)" : "");
  each(document.querySelectorAll("li[data-profiles]"), function (li) {
    var d = li.dataset.profiles;
    if (d !== "*" && d.split(" ").indexOf(p) < 0) { li.hidden = true; }
    if (li.dataset.editionOnly === "author" && e !== "author") { li.hidden = true; }
  });
  var btns = document.querySelectorAll("[data-theme-choice]");
  function show(v) {
    if (v === "system") { r.removeAttribute("data-theme"); } else { r.setAttribute("data-theme", v); }
    each(btns, function (x) { x.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(x.dataset.themeChoice === v)); });
  }
  each(btns, function (x) { x.addEventListener("click", function () { show(x.dataset.themeChoice); }); });
  show("system");
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>


=== Y ===
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
<!-- Copyright (C) 2026 the Larder software contributors. Template: gen.sh fills the list below. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Larder: start here</title>
<style>
:root {
--bg: #fffdf5;
--fg: #1b1b1b;
--help: #3a3a3a;
--btn-bg: #124a2a;
--btn-fg: #ffffff;
}
body { margin: 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 1.15rem/1.5 sans-serif; }
h1 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
ul { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
a.btn { display: block; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--btn-bg); color: var(--btn-fg); text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.3rem; border-radius: 0.4rem; }
a.btn:hover, a.btn:focus { outline: 0.25rem solid var(--fg); }
.help { color: var(--help); }
.meta { margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--help); font-size: 0.9rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Welcome to Larder</h1>
<p>This stick keeps your files. Click a button to begin. If this is your first time, click the first one.</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://setup">Set up this stick</a><span class="help">Choose a name and a PIN. Do this first.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://guide">Read the short guide</a><span class="help">Five minutes, plain words.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://network">Connect to a network</a><span class="help">Wifi or a cable.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://chat">Message other organizers</a><span class="help">Over the mesh radio or over the internet.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://docs">Write &amp; edit documents</a><span class="help">Letters, flyers and spreadsheets.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://library">Open the offline library</a><span class="help">Books, first aid, food safety. No internet needed.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://files">Sync files with your chapter</a><span class="help">Needs your chapter's server and the internet.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://editions">Books &amp; extras on this stick</a><span class="help">Extra editions this stick carries.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://close">Close this and use the laptop</a><span class="help">Nothing is lost.</span></li>
<li><a class="btn" href="larder://shutdown">Lock and shut down</a><span class="help">Your files stay safe on the stick.</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="meta">Profile: desktop. Every button here works with the mouse alone.</p>
</body>
</html>
